# Listen address. pi sessions contain code, prompts and secrets: keep 127.0.0.1
# unless you know who can reach the port.
HOST=127.0.0.1
PORT=8777
# Linux and macOS: the login checks your password with this PAM service (/etc/pam.d/<name>).
# PAM_SERVICE=login
# Turn the login off (local testing, agents driving a browser). Keep HOST on loopback.
# AUTH_DISABLED=1
# Where pi keeps its data (sessions in agent/sessions, prompts, skills). ~/.agents/skills is
# looked for next to it.
# PI_DIR=/home/me/.pi
# Where the server looks for the pi CLI (default: your login shell's PATH).
# LAUNCH_PATH=/home/me/.nvm/versions/node/v22.20.0/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
